Bundled Breeze subset for Litterbox named icons.

Source: /usr/share/icons/breeze (Debian package breeze-icon-theme).
License: see LICENSE.breeze (Debian copyright format; upstream LGPL-3.0-or-later).

Included named icons (the theme selects the nearest bundled size):
actions: list-add, application-menu, dialog-close, dialog-messages, dialog-ok,
  document-edit, document-open, document-preview, edit-clear, edit-delete,
  edit-find, go-previous, mail-archive, mail-mark-junk, mail-mark-read-symbolic,
  mail-message, mail-receive, overflow-menu, pin, list-remove, appointment-new,
  arrow-down, arrow-right, configure, transform-move, user-group, view-refresh
places: folder, user-identity
status: system-software-update

Reader/navigation additions use same-viewBox SVGs in the actions theme. The
application's `mail-archive` is a Material-style filled archive tray with a
down arrow (not Breeze archive-insert-directory's folder-plus glyph). Added
missing mail-message, dialog-close, edit-delete, and edit-clear named assets to
make the Android subset complete for QML's actual references. Their 24px
vectors scale cleanly; key phone glyphs also have 22px/32px variants. The
bundled theme provides these names on Android without relying on a system icon
theme; reader pixel-proof selects it explicitly so host icons cannot mask gaps.
